          A zero-cost pre-push branch reviewer (CLI + GitHub Action) that posts one
          sticky PR comment with a copy-pasteable fix block.
          <a href="https://glue-review.vercel.app" rel="noopener">glue-review.vercel.app</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cap-card">
        <h3>This coding agent</h3>
        <p>
          <code>cmd/glue</code> + <code>webui</code> + <code>gateway</code> in the
          same repository — daily driver locally and on AX.
          <a href="https://github.com/erain/glue" rel="noopener">github.com/erain/glue</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <section id="faq" class="border-b border-line bg-paper">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
      <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-3">
        <span class="section-num">[0x0C]</span>
        <span class="text-xs tracking-wider text-ink-muted">// faq</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mb-8 leading-snug">
        <span class="text-accent" aria-hidden="true">#</span> Anticipated questions.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-7 prose-body text-[15px] sm:text-base">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold mb-2"><span class="text-accent">?</span> How is this different from Claude Code, Codex CLI, or Gemini CLI?</h3>
          <p>
            Two ways: first, glue is model-agnostic — the same TUI, tools, and
            <code>Planner → Maker → Checker</code> loop run on Gemini, your ChatGPT
            subscription, DeepSeek, or open-weight models. Second, remote mode is
            first-class on <a href="https://github.com/google/ax" rel="noopener">AX</a>:
            uncommitted snapshots, 0-CPU suspend on questions, phone lock-screen
            buttons, a Zero-Trust Cloudflare Access web workspace, and one-command
            <code>teleport</code> back into your local TUI.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold mb-2"><span class="text-accent">?</span> How do browser and phone control work when my laptop is closed?</h3>
          <p>
             CLI dispatch (<code>glue --remote</code>) needs zero cluster services,
            and pairing <code>ntfy</code> via <code>glue job init</code> gives you
            two-way lock-screen HTTP action buttons out of the box. For a permanent
            browser URL, run <code>glue remote setup</code> once: it deploys a
            lightweight <code>glue-gateway</code> + <code>cloudflared</code> pod that
            uses <strong>0 AX worker slots</strong>, verifies Cloudflare Access JWTs
            with no second login screen, serves cached job state while sandboxes sleep,
            and wakes AX tasks only when you send a message or start a run.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold mb-2"><span class="text-accent">?</span> Why use <code>glue job teleport</code> instead of <code>git pull</code>?</h3>
          <p>
            <code>git pull</code> brings files, leaving your local coding agent blind
            to what was tried, what you answered on your phone, and which checks ran.
            <code>glue job teleport</code> safely applies the patch onto matching
            <code>--snapshot</code> branches without clobbering unrelated local WIP
            <em>and</em> hydrates a redacted <code>[user, assistant]</code> briefing
            in <code>.glue/sessions</code> so your very next TUI prompt has full context.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold mb-2"><span class="text-accent">?</span> Can I run it for free?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes: the Codex provider uses your existing ChatGPT subscription with no
            per-token API charges, and <code>openrouter/free</code> auto-picks a free
            open-weight model. For fastest coding turns (~1s median), use
            <code>gemini-3-flash-preview</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold mb-2"><span class="text-accent">?</span> What do I need to run remote AX jobs?</h3>
          <p>
            An AX cluster in your Kubernetes context (for local development on a
            workstation, <code>scripts/ax-dev/up.sh</code> stands up Kind + Agent
            Substrate + AX gVisor workers) plus <code>gh auth login</code> and a
            model API key. Jobs run the published <code>ghcr.io/erain/glue-task</code>
            image by digest — nothing to build.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
